  "notes": "USAGE:\nAlmost always appears in the set phrase {早寝|はやね}{早起|はやお}き (early to bed, early to rise). Can be used with する: {早寝|はやね}する (to go to bed early). The proverb {早寝|はやね}{早起|はやお}き{病|やまい}{知|し}らず means \"early to bed and early to rise keeps you healthy.\"\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {早寝|はやね}{早起|はやお}き: early to bed, early to rise\n- {早寝|はやね}する: to go to bed early\n- {早寝|はやね}の{習慣|しゅうかん}: habit of going to bed early\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {夜更|よふ}かし: staying up late (opposite habit)",
